er), wildcard barrels (util, component, model, view, constant), and passthrough ImageKnife exports; all target paths live under src/main/ets, outside this scope. hvigorfile.ts registers harTasks; module.json5 declares module 'common', type 'har', deviceTypes default/tablet/2in1, no abilities. build-profile.json5 (stageMode; targets default/ohosTest) enables release obfuscation via obfuscation-rules.txt (property/toplevel/filename/export obfuscation; keep FormCardEnum) and ships empty consumer-rules.txt to consumers. Keep export list, dependency pin, obfuscation keeps, and resource keys in sync.","kind":"analysis","limitations":["That every path re-exported by common/Index.ets resolves and type-checks is unproved: the src/main/ets sources lie outside this scope and were neither compiled nor fully read.","Whether the empty common/consumer-rules.txt leaves exported names exposed to -enable-export-obfuscation for downstream consumers is inferred from rule text alone; no build output or name-cache was inspected.","The '@param:dependencies.imageknife-version' placeholder substitution by a project-level configuration was not verified.","That rawfile/main_pages_list.json shortCutKey values stay consistent with ShortCutKey exported from widget/ActionUtils.ets is asserted from naming only; no intent-framework linkage was traced."],"repositoryId":"code-workshop","scopeSkillIds":["skill-scope-code-workshop-common-module-contract"],"sourceRevision":"7aa95cac4eca15e39fc6638cdf1de7db6fb70ad6"},"payloadSha256":"e46aac86ce6a1aa55667195ee3179d851b1f738c43293d9556e03ff5f42079c2","repositoryId":"code-workshop","sourceRevision":"7aa95cac4eca15e39fc6638cdf1de7db6fb70ad6"}},{"op":"insert","operation_id":"1967a507-4fde-5e50-bad6-b8bdf788a613","key":"agent-analysis-componentlibrary-hypium-verification-scaffold","row":{"id":"agent-analysis-componentlibrary-hypium-verification-scaffold","kind":"analysis","payload":{"agentProposal":{"automaticPromotion":false,"schema":"agentlab.maintainer_skill_fact_proposal.v1","sourceAssessmentSha256":"52e4e56831d0dba5d435996b90ace547b4089397e371a4d6c31ed08c48d1e598"},"dimensions":["behavior","boundary","relations","responsibility"],"evidence":[{"gitBlobOid":"85c78f67579d6e31b5f5aeea463e216b9b141048","path":"features/componentlibrary/src/ohosTest/ets/test/Ability.test.ets"},{"gitBlobOid":"794c7dc4ed66bd98fa3865e07922906e2fcef545","path":"features/componentlibrary/src/ohosTest/ets/test/List.test.ets"},{"gitBlobOid":"1fda2d887a06ee9bc44f1035799678aa6db0ad21","path":"features/componentlibrary/src/ohosTest/module.json5"},{"gitBlobOid":"165fc1615ee8618b4cb6a622f144a9a707eee99f","path":"features/componentlibrary/src/test/LocalUnit.test.ets"},{"gitBlobOid":"bb5b5c3731e283dd507c847560ee59bde477bbc7","path":"features/componentlibrary/src/test/List.test.ets"}],"id":"agent-analysis-componentlibrary-hypium-verification-scaffold","interpretation":"The scope is a symmetric hypium verification scaffold for the componentlibrary feature, split into an on-device plane (src/ohosTest) and a local plane (src/test). Both follow one contract: List.test.ets exports testsuite() registering exactly one suite; each suite ('ActsAbilityTest', 'localUnitTest') declares empty beforeAll/beforeEach/afterEach/afterAll hooks and a single case 'assertContain' (filter 0) asserting expect('abc').assertContain('b') and assertEqual on itself; the ohosTest variant adds hilog.info logging. Boundary: only @ohos/hypium and @kit.PerformanceAnalysisKit are imported; no src/main/ets component is imported, so this is a template verification surface, not component coverage. module.json5 anchors the ohosTest plane as feature module 'componentlibrary_test' (deliveryWithInstall; default/tablet/2in1). Maintenance contract: preserve the aggregator-registration pattern (new tests must be wired into testsuite()), keep suite/case names stable as discovery identifiers, mirror edits across both planes, and treat module.json5 fields as gating the instrumentation target.","kind":"analysis","limitations":["No test execution, build, or device run was performed: whether the hypium runner or hvigor test task actually discovers testsuite() from List.test.ets at this revision is unproved; the wiring is inferred only from the aggregator import pattern.","The claim that module.json5's 'componentlibrary_test' feature declaration drives generation of an installable test HAP is assumed from HarmonyOS conventions; no build-profile or consumer configuration inside the scope was read to confirm it.","The claim that these suites provide no effective regression coverage of the componentlibrary components (Index.ets exports, src/main/ets/component/*) rests on absence of imports in the five scope files; configuration-driven injection or outside-scope test code was not ruled out.","Empty lifecycle hooks implying no setup or teardown side effects is a source-text observation only; framework-level implicit behavior of @ohos/hypium hooks was not verified."],"repositoryId":"code-workshop","scopeSkillIds":["skill-scope-code-workshop-componentlibrary-verification"],"sourceRevision":"7aa95cac4eca15e39fc6638cdf1de7db6fb70ad6"},"payloadSha256":"31776c636d258ff2ab160f34bd5525acd5ec66cc4962c6583c7e2d1cdf75813b","repositoryId":"code-workshop","sourceRevision":"7aa95cac4eca15e39fc6638cdf1de7db6fb70ad6"}},{"op":"insert","operation_id":"7aedb7f6-a126-5fb4-9677-ddf628667a8b","key":"agent-analysis-hypium-test-suite-registration-surface","row":{"id":"agent-analysis-hypium-test-suite-registration-surface","kind":"analysis","payload":{"agentProposal":{"automaticPromotion":false,"schema":"agentlab.maintainer_skill_fact_proposal.v1","sourceAssessmentSha256":"52e4e56831d0dba5d435996b90ace547b4089397e371a4d6c31ed08c48d1e598"},"dimensions":["behavior","boundary","relations","responsibility"],"evidence":[{"gitBlobOid":"cdb26154e63399a77d6a9b9bd72c9057aa336c1d","path":"common/src/ohosTest/ets/test/List.test.ets"},{"gitBlobOid":"f18db0fde40224da5c2fc25064cef5cc03f6e458","path":"common/src/ohosTest/ets/test/util/ProcessUtil.test.ets"},{"gitBlobOid":"165fc1615ee8618b4cb6a622f144a9a707eee99f","path":"common/src/test/LocalUnit.test.ets"},{"gitBlobOid":"a71319f1b64f95ebe2583ce2b14b9d747e307f95","path":"common/src/ohosTest/module.json5"},{"gitBlobOid":"03d8d47af8c71849ea6fa824dc8d834e49e121dd","path":"common/src/main/ets/util/ProcessUtil.ets"}],"id":"agent-analysis-hypium-test-suite-registration-surface","interpretation":"common/src/test and common/src/ohosTest are the common module's executable verification surface. Each List.test.ets exports testsuite(), the hypium entry point registering suites. The local suite (LocalUnit.test.ets via common/src/test/List.test.ets) is self-contained, asserting only hypium expect matchers without production imports. The device suite (common/src/ohosTest/ets/test/List.test.ets) wires 33 suite functions; registration order matters because ProcessUtilTest is invoked last - its cases call ProcessUtil.exitApp/terminateAbility/killAllAbility, which its comment says terminate the test process; moving it earlier would drop later suites. Util tests read a UIAbilityContext from AppStorage under StorageKey.UI_CONTEXT (produced outside this scope), import helpers from common/src/main/ets/util, asserting non-throw guards, Promise returns, and stateful behavior (DebounceUtil counter). common/src/ohosTest/module.json5 declares feature module 'common_test' for default/tablet/2in1 devices. Contract: keep both testsuite() registrations complete and matching imports, preserve ProcessUtilTest-last ordering, and keep the local suite free of device-only imports.","kind":"analysis","limitations":["The claim that AppStorage holds a UIContext under StorageKey.UI_CONTEXT before ohosTest suites run is inferred from the tests' optional-chained reads; the producer of that key lives outside this scope and was not verified.","The claim that ProcessUtil.exitApp/terminateAbility/killAllAbility terminate the xTest process rests on the in-repo comment and the ability API names; no runtime execution, build, or device behavior was observed.","That hypium's runner discovers suites via the testsuite() export convention is assumed from the framework's usage pattern, not proven from repository source.","That the local unit suite can run host-side without device dependencies was not demonstrated by execution; it is supported only by the absence of device-kit imports in LocalUnit.test.ets."],"repositoryId":"code-workshop","scopeSkillIds":["skill-scope-code-workshop-common-verification"],"sourceRevision":"7aa95cac4eca15e39fc6638cdf1de7db6fb70ad6"},"payloadSha256":"73220266c2159685e16cc02894b5efba737778551da6741525a63e584162c623","repositoryId":"code-workshop","sourceRevision":"7aa95cac4eca15e39fc6638cdf1de7db6fb70ad6"}}],"results":[{"operation_id":"045b2151-a0d4-5420-8309-37a46cb7cf4c","op":"insert","key":"agent-analysis-common-har-packaging-contract","previous_row_version":null,"row_version":1,"deleted":false},{"operation_id":"1967a507-4fde-5e50-bad6-b8bdf788a613","op":"insert","key":"agent-analysis-componentlibrary-hypium-verification-scaffold","previous_row_version":null,"row_version":1,"deleted":false},{"operation_id":"7aedb7f6-a126-5fb4-9677-ddf628667a8b","op":"insert","key":"agent-analysis-hypium-test-suite-registration-surface","previous_row_version":null,"row_version":1,"deleted":false}]},{"path":"maintainer_skill_refresh_rounds","operations":[{"op":"insert","operation_id":"d20a7ee8-dee1-5271-b9df-afb3ab47d5dd","key":"first-four-round-31-agent-36592349984","row":{"id":"first-four-round-31-agent-36592349984","payload":{"assessment":{"path":"assessments/round-29-agent-36592349984.json","sha256":"5666182d7e425df022e95b19c46e59bb9affc1637eb8cd988d4789d093903e2b"},"automaticPromotion":false,"changes":{"added":["semantic program fact agent-analysis-componentlibrary-hypium-verification-scaffold","semantic program fact agent-analysis-hypium-test-suite-registration-surface","semantic program fact agent-analysis-common-har